# flash tool

Resolves one built target application and flashes its UF2 supplement through
picotool. The initial backend accepts only Pico SDK platforms.

--image <file.uf2> flashes a standalone UF2, including firmware produced by
external CMake projects. This mode needs no configured target lane or app
manifest. Set picotool_DIR to the installed picotool package directory.
-a/--auto-flash requests a USB reboot into BOOTSEL; otherwise the board must
already be in BOOTSEL. Both modes use the same mm.flash backend.

Host CLI regression check (records picotool arguments without a device):

```sh
./out/bin/shell --run tests/scripts/flash-image.sh
```
